# The loop is told apart in front for lists and for views. What is neither has a copy of its own, walked with guesses open: an ordinary object that keeps its elements as a list does.
# REQUIRES: entries-of-bun
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Array
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Buffer|Uint8Array
# The length is a name like any other there: its site is asked once, in front of the loop, by a read that runs no code.
# CHECK: GetValueAtSiteOrAbsent {{*}} key="length"
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=number
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# The element is read in line out of plain storage; what is not there is absent, and the turn begins again in the loop as written.
# CHECK: GetElementInStorageOrAbsent
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=number
